            <ArticleTitle>[Non-pharmacological and psychocorporal approaches to manage treatment-induced pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although healthcare workers always strive to cause the least amount of pain possible when carrying out treatment, interest in the prevention of treatment-induced pain is recent. Thereby, a certain number of non-pharmacological methods to prevent and manage treatment-related pain have proved effective in this field.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
